    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18133" root="زمل" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِمْلٌ</span></b>  <i>A load,</i> or <i>burden.</i> (K.) It occurs in a
trad. as meaning (assumed tropical:) <i>A load of knowledge.</i> (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [<i>Household-goods;</i> or <i>furniture and utensils.</i>
(Freytag, on the authority of the Deewán of
the Hudhalees.) See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَزْمَلٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا فِى جُوَالِقِكَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَّا زِمْلٌ</span> means <i>There is not in thy sack save a
half.</i> (AA, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَمِيلٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زُمَّلٌ</span>.

